IMPORT prelude

-- Charities (Institutions of a Public Character) Regulations (Cap. 37, Rg 5; originally G.N. No. S 89/2007), made under the
-- Charities Act 1994 s 42 (the Regulations' heading still cites the former number, "SECTION 40C").
-- Regulations 2 (definitions of "applicable condition" and "Sector Administrator"), 3 (conditions for approval), 4 (application,
-- refusal, period), 5 (extension), 5A (continued compliance and waiver), 6 (suspension and revocation), 9 (tax deduction
-- receipts), 10 (donation records), 11 (use of donations), 15 (fund-raising expenses, see the warning there), 16 (documents to
-- furnish), 17(7) (auditor rotation), 20 (large IPCs), 21 (offences) and 22 (financial penalty).
--
-- Edition: 2008 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 January 2025, last amended by S 1043/2024), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CA1994-RG5.txt. Regulation numbers are the body's; they agree with the arrangement
-- table. The approver of an IPC is, in these Regulations, always "the Sector Administrator", which by reg 2 means the Sector
-- Administrator of the applicant's sector or, where none has been designated, the Commissioner.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0292 (Haziq scenario, event from the Haziq scenario, event h072, 2051): "A newly
-- registered charity wishes donations to it to be tax-deductible. What status must it hold, who grants it, and on what
-- conditions?" cha-ipc.l4 answers the first two parts from the Act; this module answers the third from the Regulations.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: reg 1; reg 3(6) (who is related to an establishing entity) beyond a single Boolean; reg 3(7) (a company board
-- member counted as a citizen) beyond the count the caller supplies; the application forms and documents (regs 4(1), 5(1));
-- reg 7 (amending governing instruments) beyond its listing in reg 21; reg 8 (duty to donors) and reg 12 (accounting records)
-- beyond their listing in reg 21; reg 9(3)(a)'s statement wording and reg 9(6); reg 11(6) and (8); reg 13 (inspection and audit);
-- reg 15(2) (the Commissioner's computation directions) and the reg 15(1) formula itself, which is an image missing from the
-- deposit (see the warning at reg 15); reg 15A; reg 17(1) to (4) and (8); regs 18, 19; reg 20(1), (3) and (4); the Act's s 42(2)
-- to (5) consequences, encoded in cha-ipc.l4; the Income Tax Act 1947 ss 37 and 37AB conditions for a donation to be a "tax
-- deductible donation", which are taken here as a given Boolean; the Commissioner's or any Sector Administrator's IPC policy.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Charities (Institutions of a Public Character) Regulations`

§§ `2 -- who the "Sector Administrator" is for an applicant`

-- reg 2: "'Sector Administrator' -- (a) in relation to an applicant in a sector where a Sector Administrator has been designated,
-- means that Sector Administrator; (b) in relation to any other applicant, means the Commissioner".
DECLARE `IPC decision maker` IS ONE OF
    `the Sector Administrator designated for the sector`
    `the Commissioner of Charities`
    `the Minister as decision maker`
    `the Comptroller of Income Tax as decision maker`

GIVEN `a Sector Administrator has been designated for the applicant's sector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `IPC decision maker`
`who decides an IPC application` MEANS
    IF `a Sector Administrator has been designated for the applicant's sector`
    THEN `the Sector Administrator designated for the sector`
    ELSE `the Commissioner of Charities`

§§ `3 -- the conditions for approval`

-- reg 3(1): "An institution or fund may be approved as an institution of a public character if it satisfies the following
-- conditions: (a) it is a registered charity or an exempt charity in Singapore; (b) its governing instruments are approved by the
-- Sector Administrator; (c) its activities are exclusively beneficial to the community in Singapore as a whole and are not
-- confined to sectional interests or groups of persons based on race, belief or religion; (d) its activities meet its objectives
-- under its governing instruments and the objectives of the Sector Administrator; (e) its governing board satisfies the
-- independence requirement in paragraph (4); (ea) at least half of its governing board members are Singapore citizens; (f) its
-- governing board members are accountable for the management of donations received; (g) the appointment of its auditor is
-- approved by the Sector Administrator; (h) the approval ... is not contrary to the public interest."
-- reg 2: "'applicable condition' ... means a condition for approval under regulation 3, but excludes any condition that is waived
-- under regulation 5A".
-- READING (an inference): reg 3(1) is worded "may be approved ... if"; this encoding reads the conditions as necessary (no approval
-- without them) but not sufficient (reg 4(2) leaves a discretion to refuse). reg 5A(1) supports reading them as necessary.
DECLARE `IPC applicant` HAS
    `is a registered or exempt charity in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `governing instruments approved by the Sector Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `activities exclusively beneficial to the community in Singapore as a whole` IS A BOOLEAN
    `activities meet its objectives and the Sector Administrator's objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
    `number of governing board members` IS A NUMBER
    `number of board members not caught by reg 3(4)(a) to (d)` IS A NUMBER
    `number of board members who are Singapore citizens` IS A NUMBER
    `board accountable for the management of donations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `auditor's appointment approved by the Sector Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
    `approval not contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `condition (c) waived by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `condition (ea) waived by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `condition (e) waived by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN

-- reg 3(4): "the independence requirement is that at least half of the governing board members of the applicant must not be --
-- (a) an employee of the applicant; (b) related to any individual or entity (except the Government) that established the
-- applicant, or be such an individual or entity; (c) related to any individual who is involved in the general control and
-- management of the administration of any entity (except the Government) that established the applicant; or (d) one of a number
-- of governing board members of the applicant who are related (directly or indirectly) to each other and who collectively
-- constitute at least half of the total number of governing board members".
GIVEN `board members` IS A NUMBER
      `members not caught` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the independence requirement in reg 3(4) is met` IF
    2 * `members not caught` AT LEAST `board members`

-- reg 3(1)(ea): "at least half of its governing board members are Singapore citizens".
GIVEN `board members` IS A NUMBER
      `citizens` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `at least half the board are Singapore citizens` IF
    2 * `citizens` AT LEAST `board members`

-- reg 3(5): "an individual ... is related to another individual if the other individual is the first individual's -- (a) child or
-- grandchild; (b) sibling; (c) parent or grandparent; (d) spouse; or (e) spouse's parent or sibling."
DECLARE `Family tie` IS ONE OF
    `child`
    `grandchild`
    `sibling`
    `parent`
    `grandparent`
    `spouse`
    `spouse's parent`
    `spouse's sibling`
    `cousin`
    `nephew or niece`
    `uncle or aunt`
    `spouse's grandparent`
    `sibling's spouse`
    `no family tie`

GIVEN `the tie` IS A `Family tie`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is related under reg 3(5)` IF
    CONSIDER `the tie`
    WHEN `child` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `grandchild` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sibling` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `grandparent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `spouse's parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `spouse's sibling` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `IPC applicant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` IF
        `the applicant`'s `is a registered or exempt charity in Singapore`
    AND `the applicant`'s `governing instruments approved by the Sector Administrator`
    AND (`the applicant`'s `activities exclusively beneficial to the community in Singapore as a whole` OR `the applicant`'s `condition (c) waived by the Minister`)
    AND `the applicant`'s `activities meet its objectives and the Sector Administrator's objectives`
    AND (    `the independence requirement in reg 3(4) is met` (`the applicant`'s `number of governing board members`) (`the applicant`'s `number of board members not caught by reg 3(4)(a) to (d)`)
          OR `the applicant`'s `condition (e) waived by the Commissioner`)
    AND (    `at least half the board are Singapore citizens` (`the applicant`'s `number of governing board members`) (`the applicant`'s `number of board members who are Singapore citizens`)
          OR `the applicant`'s `condition (ea) waived by the Minister`)
    AND `the applicant`'s `board accountable for the management of donations`
    AND `the applicant`'s `auditor's appointment approved by the Sector Administrator`
    AND `the applicant`'s `approval not contrary to the public interest`

§§ `4 -- the decision on a first application, and its period`

-- reg 4(2): "Despite the applicant satisfying all of the applicable conditions in regulation 3, the Sector Administrator may refuse
-- to approve an application under this regulation, taking into account any other consideration the Sector Administrator thinks
-- fit", including past non-compliance, mismanagement, a qualified audit report, and the likely independence, governance and
-- activities of the applicant.
DECLARE `Application outcome` IS ONE OF
    `may be approved, but the Sector Administrator may still refuse under reg 4(2)`
    `cannot be approved`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `IPC applicant`
GIVETH AN `Application outcome`
`the outcome open on a first application` MEANS
    IF `satisfies the applicable conditions in reg 3` `the applicant`
    THEN `may be approved, but the Sector Administrator may still refuse under reg 4(2)`
    ELSE `cannot be approved`

-- reg 4(3): "An approval if granted by the Sector Administrator is valid for such period, not exceeding 2 years, as may be specified
-- in the approval."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest first approval in years` MEANS 2

GIVEN `years specified in the approval` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the period of a first approval in years` MEANS
    IF `years specified in the approval` GREATER THAN `the longest first approval in years`
    THEN `the longest first approval in years`
    ELSE `years specified in the approval`

§§ `5 -- extension`

-- reg 5(2): the application for extension "shall be made -- (a) at least 2 months before the expiry of the current approval; or
-- (b) within such time as may be specified by the Sector Administrator."
GIVEN `months before expiry when applied` IS A NUMBER
      `within a time specified by the Sector Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the extension application is in time under reg 5(2)` IF
    `months before expiry when applied` AT LEAST 2 OR `within a time specified by the Sector Administrator`

-- reg 5(4): "An approval under this regulation is valid for such period, not exceeding 5 years, as may be specified in the
-- approval."
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the longest extension in years` MEANS 5

§§ `5A -- continued compliance and waiver`

-- reg 5A(1): "An institution of a public character must satisfy the conditions in regulation 3 throughout its period of approval."
-- (2): "The Minister may ... waive any condition in regulation 3(1)(c) or (ea), or both". (3): "The Commissioner may ... waive the
-- condition in regulation 3(1)(e)." Both on the application of the applicant or IPC.
DECLARE `Reg 3 condition` IS ONE OF
    `condition (a) registered or exempt charity`
    `condition (b) governing instruments approved`
    `condition (c) benefit to the community as a whole`
    `condition (d) activities meet objectives`
    `condition (e) independent board`
    `condition (ea) half the board citizens`
    `condition (f) board accountable for donations`
    `condition (g) auditor approved`
    `condition (h) not contrary to public interest`

DECLARE `Waiver authority` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister may waive it`
    `the Commissioner may waive it`
    `no one may waive it`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A `Reg 3 condition`
GIVETH A `Waiver authority`
`who may waive under reg 5A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `condition (c) benefit to the community as a whole` THEN `the Minister may waive it`
    WHEN `condition (ea) half the board citizens` THEN `the Minister may waive it`
    WHEN `condition (e) independent board` THEN `the Commissioner may waive it`
    OTHERWISE `no one may waive it`

§§ `6 -- suspension and revocation`

-- reg 6(1): "The Sector Administrator shall revoke the approval ... if it appears to the Sector Administrator that -- (a) the
-- institution of a public character has ceased to operate; or (b) [it] no longer serves a purpose for the benefit of the community
-- in Singapore."
-- reg 6(2): "The Sector Administrator may suspend (for such period, not exceeding 2 years, as the Sector Administrator may specify),
-- or revoke, the approval ... if it appears ... that -- (a) [it] has failed to comply ... with the Act or any regulations made under
-- the Act at any time during its period of approval; (b) there is or has been any mismanagement, misconduct, incompetence or
-- negligence in the administration of the institution ...; or (c) such action is necessary or desirable in the public interest."
DECLARE `Reg 6 position` IS ONE OF
    `the Sector Administrator must revoke`
    `the Sector Administrator may suspend for up to 2 years or revoke`
    `no ground under reg 6`

GIVEN `has ceased to operate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no longer serves a purpose for the benefit of the community in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `failed to comply with the Act or regulations during the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `mismanagement, misconduct, incompetence or negligence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `necessary or desirable in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reg 6 position`
`the position under reg 6` MEANS
    IF `has ceased to operate` OR `no longer serves a purpose for the benefit of the community in Singapore`
    THEN `the Sector Administrator must revoke`
    ELSE IF    `failed to comply with the Act or regulations during the approval`
            OR `mismanagement, misconduct, incompetence or negligence`
            OR `necessary or desirable in the public interest`
         THEN `the Sector Administrator may suspend for up to 2 years or revoke`
         ELSE `no ground under reg 6`

-- reg 6(3)(a): "any donation made to the institution of a public character during the period of the suspension, or after the
-- revocation, does not qualify as a tax deductible donation"; (c): such a donation made "before the general public has been
-- informed of the suspension or revocation by the Sector Administrator, must (on the donor's request) be refunded to the donor
-- without any deduction."
-- reg 9(7): "An institution or a fund must not issue any tax deduction receipt -- (a) after its approval as an institution of a
-- public character has expired; (b) during the period of suspension of its approval ...; or (c) after its approval ... has been
-- revoked under regulation 6."
DECLARE `Approval state` IS ONE OF
    `never approved`
    `approval current`
    `approval expired`
    `approval suspended`
    `approval revoked`

GIVEN `the state` IS AN `Approval state`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `donations made in this state are kept out of tax deduction by reg 6(3)(a)` IF
    CONSIDER `the state`
    WHEN `approval suspended` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `approval revoked` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the state` IS AN `Approval state`
      `the public had been informed by the Sector Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the donor asks for a refund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation must be refunded in full under reg 6(3)(c)` IF
        `donations made in this state are kept out of tax deduction by reg 6(3)(a)` `the state`
    AND (NOT `the public had been informed by the Sector Administrator`)
    AND `the donor asks for a refund`

§§ `9 -- tax deduction receipts`

-- reg 9(1): "An institution of a public character must not issue any tax deduction receipt for any donation that is not a tax
-- deductible donation." reg 2: "'tax deductible donation' means a donation that qualifies for tax deduction under section 37 or
-- 37AB of the Income Tax Act 1947". With reg 9(7) above.
GIVEN `the state` IS AN `Approval state`
      `the donation is a tax deductible donation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a tax deduction receipt may be issued` IF
    `the state` EQUALS `approval current` AND `the donation is a tax deductible donation`

-- reg 9(3): a tax deduction receipt "shall -- (a) incorporate the following statement: ...; (b) state the name of the Sector
-- Administrator, where applicable; (ba) state the amount or value of the donation received; (c) be serially numbered; and (d) in
-- the case of a donation that qualifies for tax deduction under section 37AB of the Income Tax Act 1947, state that the donation is
-- made under the Overseas Humanitarian Assistance Tax Deduction Scheme."
GIVEN `incorporates the reg 9(3)(a) statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a Sector Administrator applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `names the Sector Administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `states the amount or value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is serially numbered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the donation is under section 37AB` IS A BOOLEAN
      `states the Overseas Humanitarian Assistance Tax Deduction Scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the receipt has the reg 9(3) contents` IF
        `incorporates the reg 9(3)(a) statement`
    AND ((NOT `a Sector Administrator applies`) OR `names the Sector Administrator`)
    AND `states the amount or value`
    AND `is serially numbered`
    AND ((NOT `the donation is under section 37AB`) OR `states the Overseas Humanitarian Assistance Tax Deduction Scheme`)

§§ `10 -- donation records`

-- reg 10(1): "An institution of a public character must maintain a record showing the particulars of every tax deductible donation
-- received by it." (2): "The record shall include ... (a) the receipt number (in numerical sequence); (b) the name of the donor;
-- (c) the identification number, or corporate or business registration number, of the donor; (d) the date on which the donation
-- was received; (e) the type of donation received; (f) the amount or value of the donation received; and (g) any terms and
-- conditions under which the donation was made."
GIVEN `receipt number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `donor's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `donor's identification or registration number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date received` IS A BOOLEAN
      `type of donation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `amount or value` IS A BOOLEAN
      `terms and conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donation record has every reg 10(2) particular` IF
    `receipt number` AND `donor's name` AND `donor's identification or registration number` AND `date received`
    AND `type of donation` AND `amount or value` AND `terms and conditions`

-- reg 10(3): "The record shall be maintained for a minimum period of 5 years from the end of the year of assessment relating to the
-- year in which the donation was received." (4): "year of assessment" has the Income Tax Act 1947 meaning.
-- The result is the last calendar year through whose end the record must still be kept.
GIVEN `the year of assessment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the record must be kept to the end of` MEANS `the year of assessment` + 5

-- INFERENCE, NOT READ IN THIS DEPOSIT: under the Income Tax Act 1947 the year of assessment relating to a calendar year of receipt
-- is taken to be the following year (income of a basis year is assessed in the next year). The Income Tax Act was not re-read for
-- this module; a caller who knows the year of assessment should use the function above directly.
GIVEN `year received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the inferred year of assessment for a donation received in` MEANS `year received` + 1

§§ `11 -- use of donations`

-- reg 11(2): "Where the donor has specified an intention that the donation should be used for any specified lawful purpose, the
-- donation shall be used for that purpose." (3): otherwise "according to the purpose communicated to the donor under regulation
-- 8(1)(b)(ii)". (4): where neither, "the donation may be used to fund any activity carried out by the institution". (5): "Despite
-- paragraphs (2), (3) and (4), the institution ... may use a donation for a purpose or activity only if -- (a) the purpose or
-- activity is within the objectives of the institution ... under its governing instruments; and (b) where a tax deduction receipt
-- has been issued ..., the donation satisfies the requirements of section 37(3C) of the Income Tax Act 1947".
-- (7): a donation that cannot be used under (2) to (5) must be refunded "within 4 years after the receipt of the donation" or used
-- "for such other purpose as may be approved by the Sector Administrator".
DECLARE `Permitted use` IS ONE OF
    `the purpose the donor specified`
    `the purpose communicated to the donor`
    `any activity of the institution`
    `refund within 4 years or another purpose the Sector Administrator approves`

GIVEN `the donor specified a lawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a purpose was communicated to the donor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that use is within the institution's objectives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a receipt was issued and Income Tax Act s 37(3C) is not met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Permitted use`
`the use permitted by reg 11` MEANS
    IF (NOT `that use is within the institution's objectives`) OR `a receipt was issued and Income Tax Act s 37(3C) is not met`
    THEN `refund within 4 years or another purpose the Sector Administrator approves`
    ELSE IF `the donor specified a lawful purpose`
         THEN `the purpose the donor specified`
         ELSE IF `a purpose was communicated to the donor`
              THEN `the purpose communicated to the donor`
              ELSE `any activity of the institution`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the years within which an unusable donation must be refunded` MEANS 4

§§ `15 -- fund-raising expenses (formula missing from the deposit)`

-- reg 15(1): "The total fund-raising expenses of an institution of a public character ... shall not exceed 30% of the total receipts
-- from fund-raising and sponsorships for that financial year, as determined by the following formula:" -- THE FORMULA IS NOT IN THE
-- DEPOSITED TEXT (it was an image in the PDF and pypdf did not extract it). Only its terms survive: E (total fund-raising expenses),
-- R (fund-raising receipts, net of the cost of goods sold in a fund-raising sale) and S (conditional cash sponsorships and receipted
-- sponsored property, goods and services).
-- INFERENCE, NOT READ: the formula is taken to be E / (R + S) not exceeding 30%, which is what the words "30% of the total receipts
-- from fund-raising and sponsorships" describe. Check against the PDF before relying on it.
GIVEN `E fund-raising expenses` IS A NUMBER
      `R fund-raising receipts` IS A NUMBER
      `S sponsorships` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `within the reg 15 cap on the inferred formula` IF
    `E fund-raising expenses` AT MOST 0.3 * (`R fund-raising receipts` + `S sponsorships`)

§§ `16 and 17(7) -- reporting and auditor rotation`

-- reg 16(1): "within 6 months after the close of each financial year" the IPC furnishes to the Sector Administrator its audited
-- financial statements, the auditor's reports (including on the use of donation moneys), its fund-raising and expenditure plans for
-- the next year and its annual report.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`months after the financial year end to furnish reg 16(1) documents` MEANS 6

-- reg 16(2)(a): "on or before 31 January of each year -- (a) give to the Comptroller of Income Tax ... the details of all tax
-- deductible donations for which the institution has issued tax deduction receipts in the preceding year".
GIVEN `year receipts were issued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year by whose 31 January the Comptroller must have the details` MEANS `year receipts were issued` + 1

-- reg 17(7): "An institution of a public character shall change its auditor at least once every 5 years".
GIVEN `consecutive years with the same auditor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the auditor must be changed under reg 17(7)` IF
    `consecutive years with the same auditor` AT LEAST 5

§§ `20 -- large IPCs`

-- reg 20(6): "a 'large institution of a public character' means an institution of a public character with gross annual receipts in
-- each financial year of not less than $10 million in the 2 financial years immediately preceding the current financial year".
-- (2): it "shall have not fewer than 10 governing board members" (the Commissioner may exempt under (4)).
GIVEN `gross receipts two years back` IS A NUMBER
      `gross receipts last year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a large IPC under reg 20(6)` IF
    `gross receipts two years back` AT LEAST 10000000 AND `gross receipts last year` AT LEAST 10000000

GIVEN `gross receipts two years back` IS A NUMBER
      `gross receipts last year` IS A NUMBER
      `board members` IS A NUMBER
      `exempted by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets the reg 20(2) board size` IF
       (NOT `is a large IPC under reg 20(6)` `gross receipts two years back` `gross receipts last year`)
    OR `exempted by the Commissioner`
    OR `board members` AT LEAST 10

§§ `21 and 22 -- offences and financial penalty`

-- reg 21(1): "A person who contravenes any requirement of regulation 7, 8, 10, 11 (except paragraph (8)), 12, 15A(3) or (4),
-- 16(1)(c) or (2)(b), 17(3) or (7) or 20(3) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction -- (a) to a fine not
-- exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both; and (b) in the case of a continuing offence, to a
-- further fine not exceeding $100 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction."
-- (2): a contravention of reg 15(1) is an offence with the same fine and imprisonment, and no continuing-offence fine.
-- reg 22: "A person who contravenes regulation 9(1) or (7) shall be liable to pay to the Commissioner a financial penalty of the
-- higher of ... (a) $100; (b) ... 0.4 x the total value of the donations ... which ought not to be allowed a deduction ...".
DECLARE `Reg provision` IS ONE OF
    `reg 3 conditions`
    `reg 7 governing instruments`
    `reg 8 duty to donors`
    `reg 9(1) receipt for a non-deductible donation`
    `reg 9(3) receipt contents`
    `reg 9(7) receipt after expiry, suspension or revocation`
    `reg 10 donation records`
    `reg 11 use of donations`
    `reg 11(8) telling the Comptroller of a refund`
    `reg 12 accounting records`
    `reg 15(1) fund-raising expenses`
    `reg 15A(3) or (4) directions`
    `reg 16(1)(a) audited financial statements`
    `reg 16(1)(c) report on use of donations`
    `reg 16(2)(a) donation details to the Comptroller`
    `reg 16(2)(b) annual return of donations`
    `reg 17(3) approved auditor`
    `reg 17(7) auditor rotation`
    `reg 18 conflicts policy`
    `reg 20(3) large IPC board shortfall`

DECLARE `Part VI consequence` IS ONE OF
    `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    `offence under reg 21(2), no continuing-offence fine`
    `financial penalty under reg 22`
    `no offence or penalty in Part VI`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Reg provision`
GIVETH A `Part VI consequence`
`the consequence of contravening` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `reg 7 governing instruments` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 8 duty to donors` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 10 donation records` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 11 use of donations` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 12 accounting records` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 15A(3) or (4) directions` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 16(1)(c) report on use of donations` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 16(2)(b) annual return of donations` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 17(3) approved auditor` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 17(7) auditor rotation` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 20(3) large IPC board shortfall` THEN `offence under reg 21(1), with a continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 15(1) fund-raising expenses` THEN `offence under reg 21(2), no continuing-offence fine`
    WHEN `reg 9(1) receipt for a non-deductible donation` THEN `financial penalty under reg 22`
    WHEN `reg 9(7) receipt after expiry, suspension or revocation` THEN `financial penalty under reg 22`
    OTHERWISE `no offence or penalty in Part VI`

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under reg 21(1)` MEANS
    10000 + 100 * `days continuing after conviction`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under reg 21(2)` MEANS 10000

GIVEN `value of donations that ought not to be deductible` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the reg 22 financial penalty` MEANS
    IF 0.4 * `value of donations that ought not to be deductible` GREATER THAN 100
    THEN 0.4 * `value of donations that ought not to be deductible`
    ELSE 100
